<metadata><idinfo><citation><citeinfo><origin>University of Florida - GeoPlan Center</origin><pubdate>202012</pubdate><title>Florida Composite Digital Elevation Model (DEM) - 5-Meter Cell Size - Integer Inch</title><geoform>Raster Digital Data Set</geoform><othercit>State of Florida</othercit><onlink>www.fgdl.org</onlink><pubinfo><pubplace>Gainesville, Fl</pubplace><publish>GeoPlan Center</publish></pubinfo></citeinfo></citation><descript><abstract>This data set represents a five-meter cell size Digital Elevation Model (DEM) covering the State of Florida. The elevation units are expressed in integer inches. The vertical datum is NAVD88, meters, and the projection is Albers Equal Area Conic HARN, meters. The DEM is a composite mosaic that utilizes data from several different sources. This DEM is provided with integer values, a floating-point feet DEM is available upon request. The associated layer flidar_mosaic_footprint_aug20 is a polygon layer that represents input raster footprints. Original metadatas for input rasters are included with the zip file download.</abstract><purpose>This DEM was created to be used by University of Florida - GeoPlan Center's Seal Level Scenario Sketch Planning Tool (https://sls.geoplan.ufl.edu/)</purpose></descript><timeperd><timeinfo><sngdate><caldate>2020</caldate></sngdate></timeinfo><current>publication date</current></timeperd><status><progress>Complete</progress><update>As needed</update></status><spdom><bounding><westbc>-87.6841</westbc><eastbc>-79.7542</eastbc><northbc>31.0706</northbc><southbc>24.4405</southbc></bounding></spdom><keywords><theme><themekt>ISO 19115 Topic Category</themekt><themekey>elevation</themekey></theme></keywords><accconst>None</accconst><useconst>None</useconst><ptcontac><cntinfo><cntorgp><cntorg>University of Florida - GeoPlan Center</cntorg></cntorgp><cntaddr><addrtype>mailing and physical address</addrtype><address>431 Architecture Building</address><city>Gainesville</city><state>Fl</state><postal>32611</postal></cntaddr><cntvoice>n/a</cntvoice><cntemail>data@fgdl.org</cntemail><cntpos>GIS Specialist</cntpos></cntinfo></ptcontac><native>Environment as of Metadata Creation: Microsoft [Unknown] Version 6.2 (Build 9200) ; Esri ArcGIS 10.7.1 (Build 11595) Service Pack N/A (Build N/A)</native></idinfo><dataqual><attracc><attraccr>GeoPlan relied on the integrity of the attribute information within the original data.



</attraccr></attracc><logic>This data is provided 'as is'. GeoPlan relied on the integrity of the original data layer's topology</logic><complete>This data is provided 'as is' by GeoPlan and is complete to our knowledge.</complete><posacc><horizpa><horizpar>This data is provided 'as is' and its horizontal positional accuracy has not been verified by GeoPlan</horizpar></horizpa><vertacc><vertaccr>This data is provided 'as is' and its vertical positional accuracy has not been verified by GeoPlan</vertaccr></vertacc></posacc><lineage><procstep><procdesc>The following source rasters were used for this composite. The mosaic to new dataset command was executed to combine all rasters. This list is in ascending order of priority.

Florida Everglades GAP Digital Elevation Model (Dem) - Elevation Units Feet
Digital Terrain Model for all regions in the Upper St. Johns River Basin - U.S. Army Corps of Engineers  - 2012
Manatee County FL DEM
2014 Suwannee River Water Management District Lidar: Cooks Hammock (FL)
2009-2011 NWFWMD DEM
Seminole/Big Cypress topographic elevation, 2-ft DEM, 2014
Digital Elevation Model, SRWMD LiDAR Gaps in North Central FL - 2015
Peace River Corridor LiDAR Hydrographic&amp; Topographic Survey - 2015
Continuously Updated Digital Elevation Model (CUDEM) - 1/9 Arc-Second Resolution Bathymetric-Topographic Tiles - 2014-12-09
Digital Elevation Model (DEM)- 5ft grid created from the LiDAR collected for the 2015_ITD_LiDAR project for the Miami-Dade County
Hydro-Flattened Digital Elevation Models (DEMs) Palm Beach County, Florida - 2016
For Lauderdale DEM - 2016
Martin County topographic elevation, 4-ft DEM, 2016
Osceola County topographic elevation, 3DEP, 2.5-ft DEM, 2016
Mosaic Hydro-Flattened Digital Elevation Model (DEM) Ft. Drum area 
2017 NWFWMD Lidar DEM: Escambia Santa Rosa
Hydro-Flattened Digital Elevation Models (DEMs) portions of Baker, Alachua and Levy - 2017
2017 NWFWMD Lidar DEM: Lower Choctawhatchee
City of Palm Coast Lidar Project - 2017
Upper St. Johns LiDAR; Hydro Flattened Bare Earth DEM
2018 USGS Lidar DEM: Southeast, FL
2018 USGS Lidar DEM: Southwest, FL
2018 Digital Elevation Model (DEM) data for Leon county
Continuously Updated Digital Elevation Model (CUDEM) - Ninth Arc-Second Resolution Bathymetric-Topographic Tiles - Brickell Key Selection
GeoPlan Created Using 2ft Contours

For more information on the source data please associated layer flidar_mosaic_footprint_aug20</procdesc><srcused>GeoPlan</srcused><procdate>20201209</procdate></procstep><srcinfo><srcscale>Varies</srcscale><typesrc>Online</typesrc><srccitea>GeoPlan</srccitea><srccontr>GeoPlan Center</srccontr></srcinfo><procstep><procdesc>This DEM is created based off the floating point feet version called flidar_mosaic_aug20. The following con statment was used to convert from floating point feet to integer inches: Con("flidar_mosaic_aug20" &lt; 0, Int(("flidar_mosaic_aug20"*12) - 0.5), Int(("flidar_mosaic_aug20"*12) + 0.5)) The floating point feet version is 30 GB. It's available upon request. Please contact data@fgdl.org for more information.</procdesc><procdate>20201209</procdate><srcused>GeoPlan</srcused></procstep></lineage></dataqual><spdoinfo><direct>Raster</direct><rastinfo><rasttype Sync="TRUE">Pixel</rasttype><rowcount Sync="TRUE">134257</rowcount><colcount Sync="TRUE">139276</colcount><vrtcount Sync="TRUE">1</vrtcount><rastxsz Sync="TRUE">5.432989</rastxsz><rastysz Sync="TRUE">5.432989</rastysz><rastbpp Sync="TRUE">32</rastbpp><rastorig Sync="TRUE">Upper Left</rastorig><rastcmap Sync="TRUE">FALSE</rastcmap><rastcomp Sync="TRUE">LZ77</rastcomp><rastband Sync="TRUE">1</rastband><rastdtyp Sync="TRUE">pixel codes</rastdtyp><rastifor Sync="TRUE">FGDBR</rastifor><rastplyr Sync="TRUE">TRUE</rastplyr></rastinfo></spdoinfo><spref><horizsys><planar><planci><plance Sync="TRUE">row and column</plance><coordrep><absres Sync="TRUE">5.432989</absres><ordres Sync="TRUE">5.432989</ordres></coordrep><plandu>meters</plandu></planci></planar><geodetic><horizdn>D_North_American_1983_HARN</horizdn><ellips>GRS_1980</ellips><semiaxis>6378137.0</semiaxis><denflat>298.257222101</denflat></geodetic></horizsys></spref><eainfo><detailed Name="VAT_flidar_mosaic_in_aug20"><enttyp><enttypl Sync="TRUE">VAT_flidar_mosaic_in_aug20</enttypl><enttypd>FLIDAR_MOSAIC_AUG20</enttypd><enttypds>GeoPlan Center</en